body:
Sounds like OOM (out of memory) rather than a segfault. I wonder if the `-1` is wrapping-around somewhere. 

Can you try this patch and then check `$NVIM_LOG_FILE` ?

```diff
diff --git a/src/nvim/memory.c b/src/nvim/memory.c
index b49b521bc965..3f6719daaab8 100644
--- a/src/nvim/memory.c
+++ b/src/nvim/memory.c
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@ void *xmalloc(size_t size)
 {
   void *ret = try_malloc(size);
   if (!ret) {
+    ELOG("XXX");
     mch_errmsg(e_outofmem);
     mch_errmsg("\n");
     preserve_exit();
```
